          "title": "You'll want to know: क़िस्सा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क़िस्सा — qissā — \"an anecdote; a tale\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दादा जी के पास युद्ध के बहुत क़िस्से थे। dādā jī ke pās yuddh ke bahut qisse the. Grandfather had lots of stories from the war."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क़िस्सा (qissā) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic qiṣṣa, \"a story\". It is a tale told aloud, often a true one from someone's life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
